{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the public SDK Git closure at head b05ee240783af4998b98e01c961b3135a80dc1ec, tree a558f840da28c39894d1f5e17f6747082ab5b9d1, for request cd31231e and review request 416f1e30. Verdict: APPROVED.\n\nThe head adds four commits to main 1f573145 and changes nine paths: the release guide, the Git README, four release scripts, the release plan, the implementation note and its manifest. I read the implementation note first, then the script diff, the release guide, the controls and the staged archives.\n\n## Against request cd31231e\n\n1. Git joins the plan with two exports. Resolved.\n   - `scripts/public-release.json` adds Git as the fifth of eight packages, before platform. It exports exactly `./tree-proof` and `./checkout-types`. The other ten workspace exports are listed as excluded, and Git has no root export.\n   - `publishManifest` refuses any other Git export map with `git-public-exports`. It refuses a changed exclusion list with `source-export-exclusions`.\n   - Platform's plan entry now declares its coordinated Git dependency. At this head, platform's source imports only those two subpaths: `tree-proof` in `destination-evidence-v17.ts` and `rules-policy-tree.ts`, and `checkout-types` in `evidence.ts`. The staged platform archive references only these two subpaths.\n2. A pure five-file closure. Resolved.\n   - `productionInputs` admits exactly `ascii.ts`, `checkout-types.ts`, `pure-names.ts`, `reader.ts` and `tree-proof.ts`. It refuses a changed list with `source-input-inclusions` and a missing file with `missing-included-source`.\n   - In these five files, the only imports outside the set are `@generalbusiness/dap-bytes` and `@noble/hashes/legacy.js`. None imports Node, a repository or a host transport.\n   - `outputClosure` refuses any Git `dist/` file outside the ten planned outputs with `excluded-output`. The checker refuses any other Git source input with `input-path`.\n   - The staged Git archive holds 14 regular files: the five modules as JavaScript and declarations, plus `package.json`, `README.md`, `LICENSE` and `NOTICE`. Its compiled references stay inside the five modules, `@generalbusiness/dap-bytes` and `@noble/hashes/legacy.js`. Its SHA-256 is 2218fb75, as the note states.\n3. Pinned dependencies. Resolved. Git depends on coordinated bytes and contract and on `@noble/hashes` 2.4.0, which matches the workspace manifest.\n4. No guard is weaker. Resolved. Each change adds a refusal or extends an existing exact list. The Replay exclusions, testing-output rule, bare-dependency rule and relative-closure rule are unchanged. The owning test also proves that a `gateway.js` reference, a `node:fs` import and an unplanned `gateway` module each still refuse.\n\nThe original DX-A1 carrier failure stays recorded as 2 PASS and 2 FAIL, with its own receipt.\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- The worktree is clean. `git merge-tree --write-tree` onto main 1f573145 gives the head tree a558f840.\n- Gate checkpoint 9ebdc932 has tree 269c50ef. Only the note and the manifest change from 9ebdc932 to the head. Build checkpoint 4ed3c9d9 has tree 885e1f22. Only `docs/public-sdk-release.md` changes from 4ed3c9d9 to 9ebdc932. The documents-only follow-up rule in `docs/testing.md` covers both tails.\n- I reran the owning file `scripts/public-release-modules.test.mjs` at the head, with no whole suite. It passes 4 of 4 tests.\n- The controls are real. The baseline library equals the head library. Each mutant removes one line: the `source-input-inclusions` refusal or the `excluded-output` refusal. Each mutant fails the same named test with `ERR_ASSERTION` at the assertion for the removed guard, test lines 132 and 154.\n- The manifest has SHA-256 fef91a57 and 4,632 bytes. It follows ruling 4e199bd8:\n  - all 26 listed files match by size and SHA-256;\n  - `finalization` and `operator-inputs` match their digests, and each SHA256SUMS reruns clean, with no unlisted file;\n  - the root SHA256SUMS covers all 1,581 other files, with none unlisted and none writable.\n- check-doc-links on an export of the head: 738 links, 0 broken.\n- check-notes from 1f573145: 0 warnings.\n- check-commit-messages from 1f573145: 4 checked, 0 flagged. The longest subject has 63 characters.\n- `git diff --check`: clean.\n\n## Points that do not block\n\n1. The staged Git `package.json` describes the wrong package. Its description reads \"Artroom's Git object reader, commands, push evidence, token gateway and Web HTTP provider primitives\". The archive holds no commands, push evidence, token gateway or HTTP provider. The producer copies this description from the workspace manifest. Replace it before any registry publication, with wording that matches the new README.\n2. None of the five modules imports `@generalbusiness/dap-contract`, in JavaScript or in declarations. The published Git manifest still requires it, because the plan mirrors the workspace manifest. The extra install edge costs little, but a later slice can drop it from the public plan.\n3. Writing:\n   - The implementation note uses slashes in prose: \"tool/dependency\", \"VM/container\", \"logs/times\", \"unknown/suite\" and \"source/output/declaration\".\n   - Several of its sentences are about the note itself, for example \"this note does not add them or call them wall/CPU time\".\n   - In `docs/public-sdk-release.md`, four added lines run past 79 characters. The longest, at 111 characters, starts \"excluded paths or pins still refuse\".\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe release graph now matches the source graph. Platform already imports Git's tree proof and checkout types, and the plan now says so. The release takes the five pure modules behind those two subpaths and nothing else. Exact input, export and output lists enforce that, and each list stands apart from the others. No source package changes, so the kernel, Native, the journal, host transport and storage keep their contracts. `docs/architecture.md` needs no change. Approved.\n\n## Security\n\n- The public Git package carries no Node, repository, credential or host-transport module. Three independent checks keep it so: input selection, the checker's input paths and the output allowlist.\n- The archive readback refuses nonregular, duplicate and unsafe members, and it extracts nothing.\n- The head publishes nothing to a registry and claims no consumer or deployment.\n\nPoint 1 matters before publication. A public description that names a token gateway invites readers to look for one. Approved.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThe head adds one plan entry and one inclusion list, and the inclusion list is the reverse of Replay's exclusion list. It reuses the existing producer loop, ambient declarations and compiler settings. The five-path allowlist appears in the plan, in the library constant and as test literals. That repetition is deliberate, because the test must not take its expected set from the code under test. Approved.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- The request's checks: items 1 to 4 hold in the source, the owning test, the controls, the staged archives and the sealed evidence under ruling 4e199bd8.\n\nThe landing check will follow the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4b58dcdec80b2d4a503c69b0a7a17b11698d19d9","binding":"assigned","head":"b05ee240783af4998b98e01c961b3135a80dc1ec","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:869d606b25f4b1b1864a69aff62abc2a2b7986bf\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8261c2191665ec427a50e49b467819d00a33b47a\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:869d606b25f4b1b1864a69aff62abc2a2b7986bf","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}